MView Day 20 (2026-09-28, evening)
==================================

Zoom comparison with ImageGlass (user)
--------------------------------------
The NASA world map at high zoom: ImageGlass smooths the pixels (blurred
lake, the two dark pixels smeared); MView shows each pixel as a sharp
square above 400 % and smooths only below that (mipmaps). For microscopy
the honest view: no invented values between the measured ones.

Phase F: info line and saving (user)
------------------------------------
"modify [the status line] such that the filename is left-most, then the
image dimensions wxh, then the directory and then the other stats."
- Info line: file name (without the folder), the image size in the file
  (w x h of the original, also while a quick view is shown; only once
  the image is there), the folder, then n / count, the sort order,
  skimming / loading / scanning, animated frames and status notes.
  (uMView.UpdateInfo; before: the full path first.)

"if i put something wrong in the save image directory line in the ini,
the picture is not saved. there should be a fallback dir, best the
user's documents folder."
- The save thread (uImageSaver.TImageSaveThread) now takes a fallback
  folder: if the file can't be written where asked (a wrong path, a
  missing drive, no permission), it writes the same name into the
  user's Documents folder and the status line says "saved: <file>
  (the folder <x> could not be used: <reason>)". Checked on the save
  thread, where the file is written, so the window thread still never
  touches the disk for it. SavedFileName = the file actually written
  (the paste / crop info line uses it). The settings screen's help for
  SaveImageDirectory says so.
- uConfig.UserDocumentsDirectory is now public (the fallback folder).

"upon right click - save image, there should be two choices like in
irfan view: save file, and save file as, where a save dir dialog opens."
- Menu: "Save image" (to the save folder, as before) and "Save image as
  ..." (new): a Windows save dialog, starting in the folder chosen last
  in this session (else the save folder), with the image's name as .png
  (a paste or crop: its own name with the time); asks before
  overwriting. PNG only: a .jpg / .tif / .bmp / .gif ending becomes
  .png, any other ending gets .png added. The save folder in MView.ini
  is not changed by it, and opening the dialog writes nothing. No
  fallback here: the user chose the folder, so a failure is reported.
- TMView: CanSaveImage, SaveAsSuggestion, SaveImageAs; ImageToSave and
  StartSave shared by Save, Save as (and the fallback for the debugging
  save too).
- Spec §3.1, §8.6, §9.6, §14 updated.
- Review (independent) found and fixed: a local variable "Name" in the
  form's Save-as handler (a duplicate of the form's Name property in
  ObjFPC mode: would not have compiled); Save as fell back to Documents
  even for a folder the user picked; "cell.jpg" became "cell.jpg.png";
  opening the dialog could write the Documents folder into MView.ini.

Units changed: uMView, uImageSaver, uConfig, umainform.
